From: Daniel van Vugt <daniel.van.vugt@canonical.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Jun 2025 16:22:04 +0800
Subject: monitor: Calculate fractional scaling factors using exact quotients

Here we generalise scaling factor detection to include all reasonable
quotients within the range 1.0-4.0 (which is unchanged).

In theory we are only adding some one third increments and deleting
some one quarter increments, keeping only scaling factors that divide
perfectly into the screen resolution.

In practice this also seems to yield more precise scaling factors which
you can see in the test case expectations. The old ones were often a
hundredth or a thousandth off, which may be too high a rounding error
across the size of window. And that probably explains most of the blur
that people had complained about until now.

Bug: https://gitlab.gnome.org/GNOME/mutter/-/issues/3339
Bug: https://gitlab.gnome.org/GNOME/mutter/-/issues/1135
Bug: https://gitlab.gnome.org/GNOME/mutter/-/issues/4093
Origin: https://gitlab.gnome.org/GNOME/mutter/-/merge_requests/4503
